title a check that shared the bug it was checking for
prompt Keaton said kg crypto -- and I had promised to check first whether 57.5% was a placement story or an absence.
think Ran that check and reported absence, not placement: zero trailing comments, 280 bare. It used the same narrow pattern as the meter, so it was wrong in exactly the way it was written to rule out. A check that shares the bug it checks for confirms it.
think Then opened crypto/mldsa_encode.rye to sweep and found every FIPS 204 primitive already carrying its reason -- under // invariant (precondition): and // invariant (postcondition):, a parenthetical the pattern could not read.
obs Enumerated every spelling on disk rather than patching the one in front of me: 483 lines carry a qualified label. invariant (bound) 237, (postcondition) 93, (precondition) 89, (construction) 23, bare postcondition 26, bare precondition 14, and one invariant on the callers.
obs Those are MORE faithful to the law than the bare form. TAME names three moments an assert belongs at -- construction, mutation, postcondition -- so a line naming its own category is the seated shape, and the meter had been rewarding the terser one. The pattern was written from the law's example rather than its sentence.
obs crypto was 89.8%, not 57.5%. Real gap 65, not 271. Tree 93% to 94% on the pattern alone.
think Added two control legs before sweeping: four spellings read as covered, and prose that merely names the word without a colon left uncovered. Seventeen behaviors now.
obs Then swept the real 65 with 61 blocks across 27 files -- loop bounds against the arrays they index, buffer lengths against the offsets a standard pins, canonical residues before an unreduced modular add, and the guards that make an XOF rejection loop end on adversarial output.
obs Ran both crypto guards after, as the loop rule requires: the count bijection over 82 files, and the vendored parity proving our authored Rye byte-for-byte against unmodified Monocypher and PQClean. Both GREEN.
obs crypto reads 638 of 638. Tree 95%, gap 853, against the 13,235 it carried six rounds ago.
